    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2860bf09a1070ebf24e6e6897c193bbbaba5db0728ea004fb4dacf01e445a0f7",
      "text": "Colonia Tovar is a small mountain town founded in 1843 by German immigrants. Since then, its residents have carefully preserved German traditions. Upon arrival, we’ll take a walking tour through the town, visiting the central square, the Lutheran and Catholic churches, the local market, and the Museum of the History of Colonia Tovar.\n\nAn optional agro-tour is available, including visits to a small beer and fruit wine factory, a butcher’s shop, and a tasting of the finest Venezuelan chocolate from the nearby village of Chuao.\n\nLunch in a traditional restaurant (not included).\n\nReturn to Caracas and rest at the hotel (near the airport).\n\nMeals: Breakfast",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
